From: AzallazA <54420448+AzallazA@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:59:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] helios: INT4_FP16_BLOCK32 Engram tables; KV rows backed
 only by granule padding

Engram table encoding INT4_FP16_BLOCK32 (= 16) for the int4 Engram rows of the
EXL3 3-bit pack (128 nibble bytes + eight FP16 block scales per row); the row
cache and resident-scale reader tests cover the 144-byte rows.

cache_memory: a snapshot row whose bytes lie wholly in the granule padding past
the last KV page shares no bytes with any page, so it gets an empty conflict
range instead of failing the layout ("continuation alias lacks a KV conflict
range"). Seen with TP2 row sizes below the 2 MiB granule.
