From 8b10bd961fea4d304ff8364f597089a65adbb3fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzallazA <54420448+AzallazA@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:59:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] DeepSeek V4.1: EXL3 3-bit TP2 recipe on diffbot's xmoe
 kernels (MIT), export script and CPU plan check

Serves DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash from diffbot's EXL3 3-bit pack at TP2 (two 96 GB GPUs),
recipe-local under ignition/recipes/deepseek41/exl3/ and behind FLARE_DS41_EXL3=1
(every other DS41 path unchanged):

- exl3/kernels/xmoe: diffbot's sm_120 rewrite of ExLlamaV3's exl3_moe extension
  (MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Turboderp and (c) 2026 Diffbot; LICENSE.exllamav3,
  LICENSE.diffbot, provenance and our changes in exl3/THIRD_PARTY.md). Ours: lock
  buffers from Flare core storage, and the decode-once prefill kernel's device-side
  job table (graph-capturable). Built through brrr/cuext.build (shared
  multi-source builder).
- exl3/experts.py, xmoe.py: routed experts on xmoe with TP2 rank slicing, hot
  experts in VRAM and parked (host-backed) rows staged through VRAM, declared VRAM
  rows per parked bank (FLARE_DS41_EXL3_EXPORT_HOT), per-layer hot counts, cold
  launch on a side stream, shared expert beside the router, fused decode routing
  prep, cold launch width, decode-once prefill (FLARE_DS41_EXL3_PREFILL=do).
- exl3/engram_int4.py, engram_lookup.py: int4 Engram rows (encoding 16).
- exl3/pack_reader.py, reference.py, do_reference.py: torch-free pack reader and
  NumPy reference decoders used by the tests (ours, Apache-2.0; format implemented
  from its definition, no source copied).
- checkpoint reader accepts F16/I16 tensors; tp3-tools/ds41_exl3_plan_check.py is
  the CPU plan check (--plan-only) that mirrors the b12x direct-session view checks
  and the batch executor's device-memory rule.
- tp3-tools/ds41-exl3-export-tp2.sh: the TP2 export (switches documented in its
  header; --dry-run, --plan-only; DEBUG_SERVE=1 for ignition debug-serve).
- routecount.py / routecapture.py: debug-serve only route counts and route capture
  for expert-order calibration (FLARE_DS41_ROUTE_COUNTS,
  FLARE_DS41_EXL3_ROUTE_CAPTURE; unset = nothing traced or allocated; the export
  script refuses them outside DEBUG_SERVE=1).

diffbot's vLLM patches (AGPL-3.0-only) are not used and nothing here copies them.
Tests: tests/recipes/test_deepseek41_exl3_*.py, route count/capture, engram
tables, checkpoint; tests that read the pack take FLARE_TEST_DS41_EXL3_PACK.
