Subject: [PATCH 3/5] DeepSeek V4.1 EXL3 TP2: VRAM and launch levers of the
 release export (each default off in the recipe)

Switches set by the release export (tp3-tools/ds41-exl3-export-tp2.sh documents
each; the recipe defaults stay off):

- FLARE_DS41_EXL3_WOA_SINGLE=1: keep one WO-A layout at TP2 (b12x's tile-major
  WO-A copy is never read by the WO plan; ~688 MiB per GPU). The plan check prints
  the kept copies.
- Prefill scratch: FLARE_DS41_EXL3_PREFILL_SCRATCH_ROWS (routes per decode-once
  pass), FLARE_DS41_EXL3_PREFILL_GROUPS (group-kernel groups),
  FLARE_DS41_EXL3_PREFILL_COLD_SIDE=1 (a parked layer's cold prefill launch on a
  side stream beside the decode-once kernels). The plan check prints the xmoe
  scratch per GPU.
- exl3/merges.py + kernels/merges/exl3_merges.cu (own extension, no fast-math):
  FLARE_DS41_EXL3_MERGE_TOPK (hot-map lookup folded into the fused routing prep),
  FLARE_DS41_EXL3_MERGE_EPILOGUE (routed + shared written by the MoE op),
  FLARE_DS41_EXL3_MERGE_ROPEQ (inverse RoPE + WO-A input quantization in one
  kernel; correct, no gain, off in the release). All bit-exact against the paths
  they replace.
- FLARE_DS41_EXL3_BULK_MIN_ROWS: diffbot's xmoe_bulk hot loop (MIT, headers in the
  copied files, THIRD_PARTY.md) for decode/verify graphs with >= N rows; 0 = off,
  off in the release (correct, no gain measured).
- Export script: cold launch width 16 by default (FLARE_DS41_EXL3_COLD_WIDTH=0 for
  the kernel default); FLARE_DS41_PREFILL_GRAPHS selects a subset of the prefill
  graph ladder (unset = full ladder, as released); serving note: these packages run
  with FLARE_CUDA_STACK_LIMIT=128 (the load refuses a limit below the largest
  registered kernel stack).
