Subject: [PATCH 4/5] tp3-tools/ds41_route_order.py: expert order from route
 counts measured on your own traffic

Pairs with the debug-serve route counter (FLARE_DS41_ROUTE_COUNTS, routecount.py;
the export script refuses it outside DEBUG_SERVE=1):

- snap: asks every rank process for a cumulative snapshot (start, code-a, code-b,
  prose-a, prose-b) and waits for all of them.
- drive: optional synthetic traffic from a text file (one class per call).
- build: snapshot differences -> per-layer blend of the two traffic classes'
  normalized distributions (default 0.6 class 1 / 0.4 class 2, --code-share 1.0
  for one class), rows counted selectable with --groups all|step|prefill (step =
  decode and verification rows only); writes the export's 40 layer files (router-ID
  space, pass the directory as COUNTS) and a report that compares the hot sets
  with an existing order (--release), in-sample and held-out.
- selftest: synthetic snapshots through build (CPU test added).
